{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 65, :comments ["Who is that man — walking in the field toward us. (There is hesitation regarding this verse. For was she asking about every man she encountered? And further, why is it written: 'in the field toward us'? And it appears that the verse is elliptical, and words are missing, and this is its meaning:) Who is that man walking in the field who turned from his path to come toward us?" "'That one' (הלזה) — a bet-lamed: from afar one is accustomed to speak thus, and likewise: ״בעל החלומות הלזה בא״, but when a person is close by he says: ״המן הרע הזה״."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {0 "The parenthetical marks the passage as a printed-editorial annotation; translated as presented.", 1 "Resolved צ״ל as צריך להיות לשון ב׳ ל׳, 'the expression bet-lamed'."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:45:07.641114862Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}